1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,125
How the Lungs Work.

2
00:00:02,075 --> 00:00:06,712
The human respiratory system is engineered for efficient gas exchange.

3
00:00:06,712 --> 00:00:19,012
The two lungs contain approximately 2,400 kilometers of airways branching from the trachea through 23 generations of bronchi and bronchioles, terminating in roughly 300 million alveoli.

4
00:00:19,012 --> 00:00:28,275
The total alveolar surface area spans approximately 70 to 100 square meters -- roughly the size of a tennis court -- folded within the thoracic cavity.

5
00:00:28,275 --> 00:00:37,062
Gas exchange occurs through passive diffusion across the alveolar-capillary membrane, which measures only 0.5 micrometers in thickness.

6
00:00:37,062 --> 00:00:46,212
Oxygen diffuses from alveolar air into pulmonary capillaries while carbon dioxide moves in the opposite direction, following Fick law of diffusion.

7
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:58,662
The pulmonary surfactant, a phospholipoprotein complex secreted by type II alveolar cells, reduces surface tension at the air-liquid interface, preventing alveolar collapse at end-expiration.

8
00:00:58,662 --> 00:01:04,375
Surfactant deficiency in premature infants causes neonatal respiratory distress syndrome.

9
00:01:04,375 --> 00:01:13,850
The diaphragm, a dome-shaped skeletal muscle innervated by the phrenic nerve (cervical roots C3-C5), serves as the primary muscle of inspiration.

10
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:20,512
During contraction, it flattens and expands thoracic volume, generating negative intrapleural pressure.

11
00:01:20,512 --> 00:01:28,037
Normal tidal volume at rest is approximately 500 milliliters; total lung capacity averages 6 liters.

12
00:01:28,037 --> 00:01:40,762
The brainstem respiratory centers in the medulla oblongata and pons regulate breathing automatically through chemoreceptor feedback, detecting arterial pH, carbon dioxide, and oxygen levels.

13
00:01:40,762 --> 00:01:46,875
The Hering-Breuer reflex prevents overinflation via stretch receptors in bronchial smooth muscle.

14
00:01:46,875 --> 00:01:58,512
Chronic lung diseases including chronic obstructive pulmonary disease -- the third leading cause of death globally per the World Health Organization -- asthma, and pulmonary fibrosis impair these vital mechanisms.

